  "description": "WEMNOV crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C98 H131 Cl2 N6 O15 S8 Tb4 1+,C90 H113 Cl2 N2 O17 S8 Tb4 1-,4.88(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb1A (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb3A (Tb) has 6 O neighbors; Tb4A (Tb) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.598-5.241 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.79-180.00°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula {[Tb4(μ4-OH)(TC4A)2(DMF)6(CH3OH)3(HCOO)Cl2]}·0.66CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
